al high score: Keep the F2 pung (already 3 tiles) for possible **Pung of Terminals or Honors** (1 point) and possibly **All Pungs** pattern. Discard a W tile to reduce suit variety.  \n\nBetween W1, W2, W4: W4 is a single, so discarding it loses little. W1 and W2 are pairs, useful for final pair. So discard W4.\n\nReason: Discarding W4 preserves pairs (W1 and B5) for potential pair, keeps the F2 pung for points, and moves toward Half Flush (honors + dots) since you have B5, B6, and B7 pung. W4 is a simple tile with low chow potential (only 2 left, no adjacent W3/W5 in hand). This keeps hand flexible for drawing into melds.\n\nAnswer: Play W4"}
